  "tool_adapter_policy": {
    "$comment": "Phase 2C-0 tool adapter foundation. A tool adapter is implementation/tool infrastructure (authority level ENGINE_TOOL_DEFAULTS at most): it executes an authorized capability and reports what happened. It never decides a gate, a Human Review or a lifecycle transition. forbidden_evidence_types can never be produced by a tool adapter. dry_run_evidence_types is the closed allowlist a dry run may produce: a dry run observes nothing, so every execution-observed type is excluded. A capability whose operation_class and state_model match single_writer_operation_class / single_writer_state_model must declare single_writer_required, which preserves the frozen stateful-editor policy. execution_context and an evidence candidate's capture_context both use capture_contexts: the first is the context this tool execution observed, the second the context the evidenced content was captured in. A derived candidate inherits its origin's capture_context unchanged, so media processing never upgrades the authority of its source. runtime_state_dir is non-authoritative generated state, never a record. network is the default network semantic (FORBIDDEN): GPOS provides no networking capability and an adapter takes no network destination. network_semantics is the closed set a descriptor may declare; any value other than the default is usable only by the adapter ids network_semantic_adapters lists for it, and only with a non-empty network_disclosure. TOOL_INHERENT (Phase 2C-5) means GPOS still originates no network operation and takes no URL, host, endpoint, registry, proxy or credential, but the external tool's own process tree may use the network as a consequence of running (the tool, its vendor services, supported package resolution, project and test code it loads); it claims no operating-system network confinement. tool_lease_modes (Phase 2C-6A): NONE takes no lease; EXECUTION is the frozen single-writer lease held for one execution; the SESSION modes use one SESSION-scoped lease on the same resource that outlives a single execution — SESSION_OPEN may take it only when the adapter has established its own opening conditions, SESSION_REQUIRED verifies the exact session id and canonical owner (KIND:ID) without taking or releasing anything, even for a READ_ONLY capability, and SESSION_CLOSE releases it after verification or through the attributable, explicitly authorized break operation. A SESSION lease is never judged stale from the process id of the short-lived command that took it, and never broken automatically. OUTCOME_UNKNOWN is the result status for an external operation that may have started or completed while GPOS cannot establish its final effect: it is never retried automatically and the caller must re-read the state.",
    "forbidden_evidence_types": [
      "HUMAN_EVIDENCE"
    ],
    "dry_run_evidence_types": [
      "CODE_EVIDENCE"
    ],
    "single_writer_operation_class": "MUTATING",
    "single_writer_state_model": "STATEFUL",
    "default_filesystem_scope": "PROJECT_ROOT",
    "runtime_state_dir": ".game/gpos-runtime",
    "network": "FORBIDDEN",
    "network_semantics": [
      "FORBIDDEN",
      "TOOL_INHERENT"
    ],
    "network_semantic_adapters": {
      "TOOL_INHERENT": [
        "unity"
      ]
    },
    "test_only_adapter_kind": "TEST_ONLY"
  }
